# Mega Menu — Skaflow Configuration

Architecture and conventions are in `.cursor/rules/sf-menu-architecture.mdc`.
This file is the project's configuration and current state.

Port reference: `wp-content/themes/shineon/src/sass/menu/`
Current state is this file plus `lib/class-site-header.php` and
`includes/menu/`.

## Breakpoint

**`$menu-breakpoint-key: navigation`** → 767px, not shineon's `large` (1024px).
Changing when the menu becomes mobile means editing that key in
`src/sass/menu/_variables.scss`, plus `$breakpoints.navigation` in
`src/sass/_settings.scss` if the pixel value itself changes.

## Naming

Menu locations are PHP constants in `includes/constants.php`:

| Constant | Value |
|---|---|
| `SKAFLOW_MENU_PRIMARY` | `skaflow-primary-nav` |
| `SKAFLOW_MENU_UTILITY` | `skaflow-utility-nav` |
| `SKAFLOW_MENU_THUMB_SIZE` | `skaflow-menu-thumb` |
| `SKAFLOW_MENU_THUMB_DISPLAY` | `54` (px, 2× source) |
| `SKAFLOW_MENU_THUMB_PLACEHOLDER` | `assets/images/menu-thumb-placeholder.png` |

Mobile drawer element: `#skaflow-mobile-drawer`.

## Current Sass inventory

What exists today in `src/sass/menu/`:

```
_index.scss  _variables.scss  _mixins.scss  _structure.scss
_desktop.scss  _mobile-drawer.scss  link-types/_index.scss
```

Header shell in `src/sass/header/`:

```
_index.scss  _tools.scss  _variables.scss  _base.scss  _primary-row.scss
_announcement.scss  _search.scss  _search-results.scss  _scroll-behaviour.scss
```

`@use` order in `src/sass/index.scss` is `menu` then `header`.

**Planned but not built** — `_labels.scss`, `_animations.scss`,
`_layout-patterns/` (Figma patterns A/B/C), and per-`link_type` partials beyond
the `link-types/_index.scss` stub. Treat these as backlog, not as files to
expect. Do not write a rule or an import that assumes they exist.

## What not to port from shineon

- Tab, block and cards link-type partials — not in the Skaflow Figma
- `breakpoint-menu-up` wired to `large` — wrong breakpoint here
- Generic `.header-nav` / `.mobile-menu` selectors — Woodmart collision risk
  while the legacy theme is still installed
- Hover-only mega panel reveal without `aria-expanded` / `.is-open`

